{"chunk_id": "8f2a95445b1d", "text": "Vidura advises King Dhritarashtra as Krishna arrives as a peace envoy between the Kauravas and the Pandavas. He warns the king that lavish gifts offered to Krishna are insincere and meant only to win him away from the Pandavas, who in truth ask merely for five villages. Vidura insists Krishna cannot be separated from Arjuna and urges the king to follow Krishna\u2019s counsel and make peace like a father to his sons. Duryodhana rejects this advice, arguing that honoring Krishna now would appear weak and that war is inevitable. He secretly proposes imprisoning Krishna to force the Pandavas and their allies into submission. Dhritarashtra is horrified, and Bhishma condemns the plan as wicked, foretelling destruction for those who dare oppose Krishna.\nVidura urges Dhritarashtra to accept Krishna\u2019s peace mission and grant the Pandavas justice, while Duryodhana instead plots to imprison Krishna.\nThemes: diplomacy and peace, arrogance of power, loyalty to Krishna, ignored counsel, approaching war", "vector": [-0.006725586485117674, -0.02047092095017433, -0.003331037238240242, 0.006471538450568914, 0.00810947921127081, 0.028774278238415718, -0.024014221504330635, -0.012602117843925953, -0.008350156247615814, -0.013691850006580353, 0.00893847830593586, -0.0020340553019195795, 0.01157255470752716, 0.016111992299556732, -0.02583266980946064, 0.015537041239440441, 0.04265332221984863, -0.017074700444936752, 0.03166240453720093, -0.02198183722794056, -0.010329056531190872, -0.005772906355559826, 0.01063658855855465, 0.002518752124160528, -0.025458283722400665, 0.04062093794345856, 0.010235460475087166, -0.015523670241236687, 0.0008172991801984608, -0.025993121787905693, -0.002134337555617094, 0.011010975576937199, 0.024976929649710655, 0.00023628970666322857, -0.019200680777430534, 0.011706264689564705, -0.0027193163987249136, -0.009132357314229012, 0.020216872915625572, -0.014507478103041649, 0.013665108010172844, -0.02365320548415184